# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# jbs-site — environment variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in values for local development.
# In production set these in Vercel project settings (not in source control).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the jbs-internal-portal backend API (no trailing slash).
# The chosen env var name for this project is PUBLIC_API_URL.
# Note: older planning documents (e.g. internal ADRs) may reference PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL —
# that name was not adopted. The implementation uses PUBLIC_API_URL throughout.
# When this is unset the payment application form runs in prototype / demo mode
# and submission is disabled with a clear on-screen notice.
#
# Local development (Gin default port):
PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
#
# Production (set in Vercel dashboard, not here):
# PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.buildwithjbs.com
#
# IMPORTANT — Vercel CSP prerequisite:
# The vercel.json Content-Security-Policy header currently has:
#   connect-src 'self'
# Before deploying with a live PUBLIC_API_URL you must add the API origin to
# connect-src, e.g.:
#   connect-src 'self' https://api.buildwithjbs.com;
# Otherwise the browser will block the fetch request.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web3Forms — subcontractor questionnaire email delivery
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access key from https://web3forms.com, registered to the JBS destination
# inbox (info@jbsconstructiongroup.com). Submissions from the subcontractor
# questionnaire (/client-portal/subcontractors) are emailed to that inbox.
#
# When unset, the subcontractor form renders in a disabled "Setup Required"
# state and the Submit button stays disabled.
#
# The vercel.json CSP already includes https://api.web3forms.com in connect-src
# and form-action, so no further CSP change is needed for this key.
#
# Set this in Vercel project settings (Production). Do NOT commit a real key.
# PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=your-web3forms-access-key
